All interactables are used along with React.FC

Joshua Borgueta: Setting Notification Time, Modifying Notification Settings
SetNotificationTime.py sets and saves the notification time.
SelectPreferNotifications.py edits and modifies notification settings, as well as enabling and disabling activation.

Paul Peters: Location Geocoding, Weather API
weather_service.py takes the user's city and optional country code and converts it into latitude and longitude using the Open-Meteo Geocoding API.
The coordinates are then used to retrieve current weather conditions and a three-day forecast from the Open-Meteo Weather API.
weather_service.py organizes the weather data, including temperature, humidity, precipitation, and evapotranspiration, into a structured format that can be used by other modules for watering recommendations.
test_weather.py contains three automated unit tests to verify the weather module's functionality.
The module also handles invalid city inputs by displaying an error message when a location cannot be found.

Cole Franks: Create Account, Daily Settings
create_account.py handles user registration, input validation, and inserts new user credentials into a SQL database.
daily_settings.py manages daily watering schedule preferences, client-side tab state memory, and overwrites daily settings in a SQL database.
both have their own HTML pages that link to the modules and send inputs to them.

Diep Tran: Add Prefer Time, Connect Sprinkler, Change Sprinkler, Display Advice
sprinkler_service.py: handles adding new sprinkler, removing sprinkler, editing sprinkler's name
watering_advisor.py: based on criteria (soil_moisture, forecase_rain in mm, and rain_probability), calculate whether the user should water their lawn that day, then print back to the user the decision. If their soil's water content is high -> no need for watering, if there's a high probability of rain or heavy rain later on -> hold on the watering, and for invalid or missing information, output to tell the user which data is missing.
watering_schedule.py: allows users to input their preferred time for daily watering, as well as auto change the schedule for daylight savings time adjustment

